## WORKED EXAMPLE

**Question**: "Which suppliers have the highest quality rating?"

**Step 1 — Analyze**: Primary concept = "quality rating". Secondary = "suppliers". What data sources could contain quality information? Quality scores, defect rates, inspection results, compliance records, audit outcomes.

**Step 2 — First pass**: `Supplier Name` (suppliers), `Quality Score` (quality rating — direct match).

**Step 3 — Second pass**: `Inspection Result` (description says "quality inspection outcome" — contains "quality"), `Defect Count` (description says "number of defects found" — defects are a quality measure), `Compliance Status` (description says "regulatory compliance rating" — compliance relates to quality).

**Step 4 — Apply rules**: Include all 5 relevant columns. No duplicates, no unnecessary breakdowns. `Total Quality Score` exists, so do NOT also select individual quality sub-scores.

